{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-27T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Water, sunlight and lush greenery come together at Rainbow Falls in Hilo, on Hawaii's Big Island. Here, the Wailuku River plunges  24 metres over a lava ledge, sending mist into the air as it reaches the pool below. On sunny mornings, that mist can catch the light and produce the colourful rainbows that gave the falls their name.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RFHilo_ROW7802013714_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RFHilo_ROW7802013714_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Rainbow Falls on the Wailuku River, Hilo, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© Peter Unger/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261126_RFHilo\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rainbow+Falls+Wailuku+River+Hawaii&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261126_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261126_RFHilo"},"Ssd":"20261126","Name":"RFHilo","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7802013714","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 26 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Snow transforms Utah's Bryce Canyon National Park, blanketing the landscape in white while its fiery orange-red hoodoos rise above the snowy terrain. Seen from Sunset Point, one of the park's most famous overlooks, these fantastical shapes are part of the Claron Formation, whose limestone was deposited about 50 million years ago and later shaped by weathering and erosion. Because much of the park rises above 2,440 metres, snow can arrive as early as October. In today's image, snow clings to the canyon's ridges and spires while mist drifts across the cliffs, creating an iconic winter scene in the American Southwest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SunsetPoint_ROW8066208115_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SunsetPoint_ROW8066208115_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Sunset Point, Bryce Canyon National Park, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© Colin D. Young/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261125_SunsetPoint\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bryce+Canyon+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261125_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261125_SunsetPoint"},"Ssd":"20261125","Name":"SunsetPoint","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8066208115","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 25 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As Britain's only native squirrel species, red squirrels thrive in Scotland's Cairngorms National Park. An important refuge, the park offers ancient Caledonian pine forests and newer conifer woodlands, with plentiful habitat and food for squirrels foraging for Scots pine seeds, nuts and other tasty morsels year-round. In today's image, a red squirrel is perched amid warm orange and yellow leaves, looking right at home as it ponders its next move in the Scottish Highlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CairngormsSquirrel_ROW7336059810_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CairngormsSquirrel_ROW7336059810_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Red squirrel in Cairngorms National Park, Highlands, Scotland","Copyright":"© Scotland: The Big Picture/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261124_CairngormsSquirrel\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Eurasian+red+squirrel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261124_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261124_CairngormsSquirrel"},"Ssd":"20261124","Name":"CairngormsSquirrel","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7336059810","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 24 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today's image shows the gradual coiling of a young fiddlehead's tip, echoing the geometric patterns seen throughout nature. In mathematics, the Fibonacci sequence follows a similar progression, each number formed by adding the two before it: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 and so on. Eventually the young fern frond shown here will unfurl as it grows, but elsewhere in the plant world, the sequence will continue to appear in the spiralling arrangements of sunflower heads, pinecones, succulents and pineapples.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FibonacciFern_ROW6425813382_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FibonacciFern_ROW6425813382_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Fiddlehead fern","Copyright":"© Reza Saputra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261123_FibonacciFern\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Fiddlehead+fern&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261123_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261123_FibonacciFern"},"Ssd":"20261123","Name":"FibonacciFern","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6425813382","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 23 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off Greenland's west coast, enormous icebergs drift through the cold waters, creating a landscape that's constantly changing. Many originate from the nearby Jakobshavn Glacier, one of the world's fastest and most active glaciers. The surrounding Ilulissat Icefjord, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, lies about 250 kilometres north of the Arctic Circle. Here, towering blocks of ice break away and begin their slow journey towards the open sea, forming one of Greenland's most remarkable natural sights.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GreenIceberg_ROW6926688504_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GreenIceberg_ROW6926688504_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Icebergs, Ilulissat, Greenland","Copyright":"© James Yu/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261122_GreenIceberg\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ilulissat+Greenland&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261122_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261122_GreenIceberg"},"Ssd":"20261122","Name":"GreenIceberg","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6926688504","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 22 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bathed in a sun-kissed glow, Nice is a patchwork of terracotta rooftops, historic churches and pastel façades along the French Riviera, as seen in today's image. Founded by ancient Greeks and long connected to the Italian royal House of Savoy, Nice officially became part of France in 1860. Today, that layered past remains visible throughout the coastal city in the south of France, where old-world architecture meets the blue Mediterranean waters and sunlit hills of the Côte d'Azur.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RedNice_ROW6800043418_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RedNice_ROW6800043418_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Nice, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France","Copyright":"© Siripong Kaewla-iad/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261121_RedNice\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Nice+France&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261121_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261121_RedNice"},"Ssd":"20261121","Name":"RedNice","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6800043418","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 21 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Kvaløya in Troms, Northern Norway, humpback whales move through the cold Arctic waters in search of a proper feast. They visit this region during the winter months, following migrating herring into the fjords. Humpbacks are famous for bubble-net feeding, a remarkable hunting technique in which whales blow rings of bubbles to corral fish before lunging upwards, open-mouthed, to catch their prey. In today's image, a humpback slips beneath the icy waves under a glowing pastel sky, capturing a moment of tranquility in Norway's wild north.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Megaptera_ROW6602236016_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Megaptera_ROW6602236016_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Diving humpback whale, Kvaloya, Troms, Northern Norway","Copyright":"© Espen Bergersen/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261120_Megaptera\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=humpback+whales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261120_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261120_Megaptera"},"Ssd":"20261120","Name":"Megaptera","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6602236016","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 20 日"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Deep within Ranthambore National Park, Indian banyan trees take root. Let the other trees grow from the ground up; banyan seeds sprout on branches, buildings or ruins, dropped by passing birds. Once there, their aerial roots descend to the ground, slowly thickening into branch-supporting trunks. This allows the fig trees to spread over huge areas, providing fruit and shelter for wildlife, and welcome shade for people.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FicasBenghalensis_ROW9163932137_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FicasBenghalensis_ROW9163932137_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Indian banyan tree on arch ruin, Ranthambore National Park, India","Copyright":"© Vincent Grafhorst/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261203_FicasBenghalensis\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ranthambore+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261203_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261203_FicasBenghalensis"},"Ssd":"20261203","Name":"FicasBenghalensis","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9163932137","FullDateString":"2026 年 12月 月 3 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Dramatic limestone cliffs rise above the turquoise lagoons around Coron Island, creating one of the Philippines’ most distinctive landscapes. Hidden among the rock formations are calm stretches of water, surrounded by lush tropical vegetation. The area is part of the Calamian Islands, where towering limestone karst formations meet the warm waters of the Philippine archipelago. Visitors can explore secluded lagoons by boat or kayak, swim in sheltered waters and discover quiet coves tucked between the cliffs.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LimestonePhilippines_ROW9042129941_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LimestonePhilippines_ROW9042129941_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lagoons and limestone cliffs, Coron, Palawan, Philippines","Copyright":"© R.M. Nunes/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261202_LimestonePhilippines\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Coron%2c+Palawan&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261202_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261202_LimestonePhilippines"},"Ssd":"20261202","Name":"LimestonePhilippines","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9042129941","FullDateString":"2026 年 12月 月 2 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Waddling across the vast and wind-swept ice fields, emperor penguins are one of Antarctica's most iconic species. While humans here are restricted to scientific research stations and expeditions, emperor penguins have learned to adapt to the frozen continent's inhospitable climate. The emperors' dense feathers and fat reserves help to keep them warm. And this sociable bunch know how to share – they huddle together in groups, shuffling around so each gets a turn in the centre, where it's warmest. Thousands of scientists travel here each year to conduct research in various fields, including climate change – the biggest threat to the sea ice on which emperor penguins rely to breed and raise their young.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.EmperorAntarctica_ROW7975409903_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.EmperorAntarctica_ROW7975409903_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Emperor penguins, Queen Maud Land, Antarctica","Copyright":"© Stefan Christmann/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261201_EmperorAntarctica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Emperor+penguins&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261201_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261201_EmperorAntarctica"},"Ssd":"20261201","Name":"EmperorAntarctica","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7975409903","FullDateString":"2026 年 12月 月 1 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"We're looking out over one of Scotland's most otherworldly landscapes, formed by ancient landslides on the Isle of Skye. Millions of years ago, layers of heavy lava settled here on top of soft clay and rock, before gradually sliding down towards the sea. It left steep slopes, hidden plateaus and jagged rock formations along the Trotternish Peninsula, which forms Skye's northernmost tip.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.QuiraingSkye_ROW8702099917_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.QuiraingSkye_ROW8702099917_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"The Quiraing, Trotternish, Isle of Skye, Scotland","Copyright":"© Matt Anderson Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261130_QuiraingSkye\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=The+Quiraing+Isle+of+Skye+Scotland&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261130_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261130_QuiraingSkye"},"Ssd":"20261130","Name":"QuiraingSkye","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8702099917","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 30 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lit by streetlights as it crosses this narrow stretch of the Norwegian Sea, Sommarøy Bridge is the only road onto the small fishing island that shares its name. From a distance, with its white sand beaches and turquoise waters, you might think you were somewhere tropical. But Sommarøy sits north of the Arctic Circle, and those are icy waters you're crossing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SommaroyBridge_ROW8783121645_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SommaroyBridge_ROW8783121645_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Sommarøy Bridge from above, Tromso, Norway","Copyright":"© Roberto Moiola/Sysaworld/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261129_SommaroyBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sommar%c3%b8y+Norway&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261129_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261129_SommaroyBridge"},"Ssd":"20261129","Name":"SommaroyBridge","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8783121645","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 29 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"This autumnal view from Letná Park looks out over Prague, which grew up along the banks of the Vltava River in Czechia. In today's image, the river winds its way through the historic Old Town and Malá Strana districts, beneath Mánes Bridge in the foreground. Many beautiful bridges now span the Vltava, but for centuries there was only one, Charles Bridge, pictured second from the bottom. Its first stones were laid in 1357 during the reign of Charles IV and until 1841, it was the only way to cross the river on foot. Today its stone arches, gothic towers and statues lining the bridge draw large crowds, so tourists are advised to get there by dawn for the best photographs. Or they could walk on to the next crossing, Legion Bridge, which is less crowded and offers beautiful views of the National Theatre, Prague Castle and its busier neighbour.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VltavaPrague_ROW8370257581_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VltavaPrague_ROW8370257581_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Old town and Vltava River, Prague, Czechia","Copyright":"© Lara_Uhryn/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261128_VltavaPrague\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Prague+bridges&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261128_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261128_VltavaPrague"},"Ssd":"20261128","Name":"VltavaPrague","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8370257581","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 28 日"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Hidden within an ancient sandstone landscape, Face Canyon is one of 96 canyons stretching out from Lake Powell in the US state of Utah. Many are far from roads and would be hard to reach if they hadn't been flooded by the lake, created in 1963 during the construction of the Glen Canyon Dam. The lake's waters back up nearly 300 kilometres, along creeks and canyons which you can explore by boat, kayak or personal watercraft.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FaceCanyon_ROW8227302617_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FaceCanyon_ROW8227302617_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Butte at sunset, Face Canyon, Lake Powell, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© Jeff Foott/Minden","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261127_FaceCanyon\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Powell&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261127_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261127_FaceCanyon"},"Ssd":"20261127","Name":"FaceCanyon","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8227302617","FullDateString":"2026 年 11月 月 27 日"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"今日圖片","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"深入了解","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"快速事實:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"最近的首頁圖片","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"{0}的首頁圖片","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"在歷史上的這一天","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"在這一天的 {0}，{1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"分享今日 Bing 首頁","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"下載此影像。禁止將此影像用於桌布以外的用途。","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"此圖片無法下載作為桌布。","LOC_HOMEPAGE_INFO_TEXT":"資訊","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK":"https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2127455","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK_TEXT":"取得新的 Bing Wallpaper 應用程式","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_TOB":"Bing 上的熱門項目","LOC_HOMEPA